{
  "version": 2,
  "rules": [
    "Same canonical JSON and sha256 rules as evidence-vectors.json (version 2).",
    "A non-integer measurement is carried as <field>_milli: floor(value * 1000) computed in IEEE double arithmetic (Math.floor in TypeScript, math.floor in Python); null stays null.",
    "sensor_readings rows have no id column: the evidence id is '<parcel_code>|<sensor>|<ts>' with ts normalised like every timestamp.",
    "weather_cache: forecast_days and forecast_precipitation_milli come from forecast_json.time and forecast_json.precipitation_sum in order; a null forecast_json gives two empty arrays; other forecast fields are left out.",
    "market_data is shared by every cooperative; its loader does not filter by cooperative."
  ],
